===============================================================================
                       VERNICHTUNG CONTRIBUTING GUIDE
===============================================================================

Hey everyone,
Thanks for checking out Vernichtung!

If you want to help push this project forward, here is what you need to know.

WHAT IS THE GOAL?
-----------------
Vernichtung exists to be a completely independent, reconstruction
of the id Tech 1 architecture under a permissive, non-viral license.

LICENSING & COPYLEFT
--------------------
This project is officially released under the 3-Clause BSD License. 

By contributing code, bug fixes, or patches here, you agree that your work 
will be under the same BSD license. We do not accept viral copyleft code because 
we want to keep this project completely permissive (and fulfill John Carmack's 
and other devs wishes).

THE CODE STRUCTURE
------------------
The engine is split into isolated modules so it is easy to navigate:
* u_archive.c : Hardened WAD loading, parsing, and data flattening.
* i_video.c   : Framebuffers, SDL2 textures, and that cool screen melt.
* i_input.c   : Keyboard inputs and mouse sensitivity handling.
* p_physics.c : Player movement, sliding wall collisions, and stairs.
* r_main.c    : 2.5D software rendering loop and BSP node traversal.
* main.c      : Core loop, timing gates, and window resizing events.

If you add anything, make sure it stays modular and includes defensive array 
boundary checks. And make sure it has comments to explain!

AI ASSISTANT & LLM CODE POLICY
------------------------------
I used AI code as a tool to help make Vernichtung. AI coding is fine, but if you 
use an AI assistant to help you write patches for this engine, you MUST follow 
my strict rules:

1. Test the code on your device first. Do not blind-paste things.
2. AI bots are completely banned from signing their own names to commits.
3. A real human (you!) must review the code manually before sending it over.
4. LLMs are tools, not the developer. You are the developer.

If you don't like AI at all, feel free to fork Vernichtung or block me.

WHAT NEEDS FIXING RIGHT NOW?
----------------------------
* The Vertical Texture Bug: Walls stretch and distort vertically when you get 
  too close or look around, so it is a perfect first issue if you want to tackle 
  the r_main.c column math!
* PWAD support: We need "-file" support to load custom patch WADs.
* MUS-to-MIDI translator: A clean-room layer to feed audio into Nuked-OPL3 or 
  FluidSynth for music.

HOW TO SUBMIT WORK
------------------
1. Fork the repo and make your changes on a clean branch.
2. Make sure it compiles without warnings on GCC or Clang.
3. Keep your commits clean and explain what your code updates.
4. Open a Pull Request.

I don't know how many people are going to contribute, but even small fixes 
help a ton. 

Ok, stay safe out there.

Have fun.

- Rafael
